      "text": "Maximum likelihood estimates assign zero probability to any bigram that never appeared in the training data, so a sentence containing one unseen bigram gets probability zero. Add-one (Laplace) smoothing adds one to every bigram count and adds the vocabulary size V to the denominator, redistributing probability mass from seen to unseen events so that no probability is zero.",
